cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these workflows, please cite them as below."
title: "Analytical workflows for product testing with users in agriculture. AI-ready reasoning from rankings to decisions"
abstract: >-
  Tested R workflows for the main questions asked of tricot, on-farm ranking
  and consumer concept testing data, from Bioversity International and
  Wageningen University. Each use case starts from a scientific question,
  links to a decision record with the default method, its alternatives and
  what the results cannot support, and runs with synthetic data and tests.
  The repository works as a Claude skill and is readable by people and other
  AI tools.
type: software
